21,0 $ A. Branches buffy yellow, pale ochraceous yellow to fleshy buff when young; tips pale chartreuse-yellow but often blushing to onion skin pink if exposed to cold, dry air; vernal; spores Lm =9.95 µm (8.3-11.5 × 3.6-4.3 µm) $ R. rasilispora var. rasilispora
